      {
        "id": 60106,
        "name": "j1hopki1",
        "username": "j1hopki1",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/58f4c7/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-07-30T02:27:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I understand that there are cases where they would not be the same. I was merely trying to suggest how to make the rules clear if the designers wanted to make it clear that her advanced redirect rule applied before her normal prevent rule.</p><p>However, it's a moot point because the designers have now given official rulings that actually her normal prevent rule does happen before her advanced redirect rule is triggered. I am not happy about the ruling because it means that her advanced rule only applies once after she flips. I think that does not add much interest or strategy to her side B.</p>",
